<!-- PRIVACY -->
<section id="privacy" style="background:#00111F;color:#EAF2F6;margin-top:100px">
  <div class="wrap" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,440px),1fr));gap:64px;align-items:center;padding-top:110px;padding-bottom:110px">
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px">
      <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#2ECC71;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase">Privacy</span>
      <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(34px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-0.03em;font-weight:700;color:#FFFFFF">Your messages stay on your phone</h2>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#9DB3C2">Altus reads bank alerts so you don't have to type them. This is exactly what happens to them.</p>
      <ul style="margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55">
        <li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="#2ECC71" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex:none;margin-top:2px"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Each SMS is read on your phone. The text of a message is never sent anywhere.</li>
        <li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="#2ECC71" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex:none;margin-top:2px"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Only business senders are read, and a sender Altus doesn't know needs your OK first. Messages from people, OTPs and promotions are skipped.</li>
        <li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="#2ECC71" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex:none;margin-top:2px"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>A statement password is used once to open the file and never stored. The file is deleted after it's read.</li>
        <li style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="#2ECC71" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="flex:none;margin-top:2px"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"></path></svg>Export your transactions as CSV, or delete your account from Settings any time. Your own data goes with it. Groups you shared keep your name, so the others' balances stay right.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/download#permissions" style="color:#2ECC71;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;min-height:44px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center">What Altus asks for, and why <span aria-hidden="true" style="margin-left:8px">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0;align-items:stretch">
      <div style="background:#071D30;border:1px solid #14324B;border-radius:24px;padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between"><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#9DB3C2">ON YOUR PHONE</span><span style="font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#7EE2A8;background:#0D3B2A;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:999px">Parser runs here</span></div>
        <div style="background:#0A3354;border-radius:14px;padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#9FC3D8;text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,138,128,.7)">Rs.450.00 debited from a/c **4821 to SWIGGY on 28-11-26. UPI Ref 6331. Not you? Call 1800…</div>
